    <statement><p>Suppose that <m>\displaystyle f(x,y,z)= x^2yz-xyz^3</m> is a function of three variables.</p>
<p><alert> 1.</alert> Find the gradient of <m>f(x,y,z).</m></p>
<p>Answer: <m>\nabla f(x,y,z) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> 2.</alert> Evaluate the gradient at the point <m>P(-2,1,1).</m></p>
<p>Answer: <m>\nabla f(-2,1,1) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert> 3.</alert> Find the rate of change of <m>f(x,y,z)</m> at <m>P</m> in the direction of the vector <m>\mathbf{u} = \left\langle 0, \frac{4}{5},-\frac{3}{5}\right\rangle .</m></p>
<p>Answer: <m>D_{\mathbf{u}}\,f(-2,1,1) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;2xyz-yz^{3},x^{2}z-xz^{3},x^{2}y-3xyz^{2}\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
